Well, that is in fact not actually the case.

NetHack's root is the game of rogue, in which there was a very strict
time pressure: FOOD. That commodoty was so scarce in rogue, that you
*had to* play fast, or you would die of starvation.

If I recall correctly, in the earlier versions of NetHack (and Hack)
food concerns were also much stricter than nowadays. I believe that you
couldn't eat corpses, food distribution might have been different,
prayer wasn't as effective as it is now, and there might have been more
reasons.

This lack of food *did* put a pressure on the game (not just the mid
game).

Obviously, though, the Dev Team have decided, in their infinite wisdom,
that this was too difficult, and have changed this to allow for a longer
and easier game.

